<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Faint gear/blueprint linework scattered across the hatch tile's background,
  behind the pipe - thin schematic circles with crosshair ticks, small gear
  outlines, a dimension line, scattered bolt dots, all in one muted tone at
  low opacity. No rat drawn into it on purpose - the tile already has its own
  rat riding the cart, and this is background texture only.

  Matched by eye to the reference rather than extracted from a resource:
  there is no standalone texture asset anywhere in this app to pull a
  drawable from - the closest precedent, miller_pic.jpg, is a flattened JPEG
  with its own linework baked into the same pixels as the artwork, not a
  separate layer. This redraws the same motifs as their own small vector at
  low opacity instead.
-->
